hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"146","Ahmad bin Abd al-Rahman bin Wahb told me, my uncle told me, Ibn Lahi’ah and Jabir bin Ismail al-Hadrami told me, on the authority of Aqeel bin Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you wakes up from In his sleep, he should not put his hand into the vessel until he has washed it three times, for he does not know where his hand has spent the night, or where his hand has wandered.” Then a man said to him: Did you see if it was a basin? He said: So Ibn Omar counted it, and said: I told you about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and you say: Did you see if it was a basin?! Abu Bakr said: Ibn Lahi’ah is not among those whose hadith I narrate in this book if he narrates alone, but I only narrated this report, because Jabir bin Ismail is with him in the chain of transmission"
